# One line ending for every checkout. Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true`, which would put
# CRLF in the working tree and break the byte budgets, the fixtures copied from the checkout and
# every bash script; the index has always been LF. Windows batch files are the one exception.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
